{"name":"Candytuft","hex":"#edc9d8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"candytuft","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of the genus Iberis of flowering plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/candytuft"}],"entries":[{"title":"Iberis","blocks":[{"text":"Iberis, commonly called candytuft, is a genus of flowering plants belonging to the family Brassicaceae. It comprises annuals, evergreen perennials and subshrubs native to the Old World. Species are native to the Mediterranean basin, Western Asia, the Caucasus, and western Europe. The name \"candytuft\" is not related to candy, but derives from Candia, the former name of Iraklion on the island of Crete."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Iberis%2Bsempervirens.jpg/330px-Iberis%2Bsempervirens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iberis","wikidata":"Q158380"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.398125},{"title":"Evergreen candytuft","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Evergreen_candytuft.jpg/500px-Evergreen_candytuft.jpg","ratio":0.9996498599439776,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Evergreen_candytuft.jpg","share":0.089375},{"title":"Light Coloured Candytuft Flowers - July 2024","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Light_Coloured_Candytuft_Flowers_-_July_2024.jpg/500px-Light_Coloured_Candytuft_Flowers_-_July_2024.jpg","ratio":0.9405,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Light_Coloured_Candytuft_Flowers_-_July_2024.jpg","share":0.063125},{"title":"Iberis or Candytuft from lalbagh 2086","image":"https://thumb.wik